IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `colc-common`

-- Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986 (SA), with the Cost of Living Concessions Regulations 2020 -- the seat-neutral
-- core: who occupies a home as an owner or tenant, who is an eligible person, who is entitled to the cost of living
-- concession and how much it is, the water rates remission, and the duties to tell the Minister and to refund.
--
-- ACTORS (the text's own): a person and an "eligible person" (s 3), a "ratepayer" (s 4, reg 5), the Minister. The
-- concession holder's questions are in colc-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this module and restates no rule.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Act: s 2(1) ("residential premises", "rates", "approved aged persons housing scheme"), s 2(2)
-- (occupying as an owner), s 2(3) (occupying as a tenant), s 3 (eligible person on 1 July; entitlement to the payment),
-- s 4(1), (3) (remission of rates, in the opinion of the Minister), s 7 (no interest, fine or penalty), s 8(2)-(4)
-- (tell the Minister; refund; maximum penalty $2 500; recoverable as a debt). Regulations: reg 3(1) ("prescribed card",
-- "prescribed payments", "low income earner", "relevant asylum seeker", "water rates", "spouse", "domestic partner"),
-- reg 3(2) (prescribed capacity), reg 3(3)-(4) (indexation and its floor), reg 4 (prescribed occupier classes), reg 5
-- (water rates remission), reg 6 (eligible classes), reg 7 (eligibility requirements, the Minister's split, Switch for
-- Solar), reg 8 (the amount).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 5 (delegation), s 6 (the Treasurer pays rating authorities), s 8(1) (false or misleading statements:
-- an offence, $2 500 or 3 months, outside this encoding's scope), s 9 (regulations), Schedules 1 and 4 except as the
-- definition of "rates" uses them; the means test the Minister determines under reg 5(1)(c) (its outcome is an input).
--
-- EDITION. Act: Open Australian Legal Corpus text as at 2015-07-01 (scraped 2024-09-13), deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/cost-of-living-concessions-act-1986.txt. Regulations: corpus text as at 2025-01-01
-- (scraped 2025-03-10), deposited at
-- ../../../cost-of-living-concessions-regulations-2020/registers/source-bundle/cost-of-living-concessions-regulations-2020.txt.
-- Neither is the official text; both may be out of date.
--
-- COVERAGE. Regulation 8 and the reg 5(5) amounts were substituted from 1 July 2024 (49/2024), so a financial year
-- beginning before 2024 answers `not covered`. Later years are covered, with the CPI figures and the previous year's
-- amounts as inputs (reg 3(3)-(4)); the Regulations may have changed since 2025-01-01.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken
-- from the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0); each text is as at the corpus scrape and may be out of date.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986 and Regulations 2020 -- the core`

§§ `s 2(2), (3), reg 3(2), reg 4 -- occupying a home as an owner or as a tenant`

-- s 2(2)(b): the capacities of an owner. (i) "a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession";
-- (ii) "a sole or joint proprietor of a Crown lease or Crown under lease"; (iii) "a purchaser of an estate in fee
-- simple under an agreement for sale and purchase where the purchase price is payable in more than 2 instalments";
-- (iv) "the occupier under an agreement to occupy provided that (A) no rent is payable; and (B) the tenure is for the
-- life of the occupier and not subject to earlier determination except by the occupier; and (C) the occupier is liable
-- for all rates and taxes" (the three provisos are folded into the choice); (v) a joint proprietor with others who
-- own, or a shareholder in a body corporate that owns, "a block of home units or other group residential premises";
-- (vi) "a lessee or licensee of land other than Crown land under a lease or licence that extends for 5 or more years
-- and under which the premises occupied by the person on that land remains the property of that person"; (vii) "the
-- occupier of a house or residential unit in an approved aged persons housing scheme"; (viii) "a beneficiary under an
-- estate entitling the person to occupy the premises in 1 of the capacities referred to in subparagraphs (i) to (vii)";
-- (ix) "a person of a class prescribed by the regulations": reg 4(1)(a) spouses and domestic partners of persons in
-- (i)-(vii); (b) persons granted a right of occupancy under a residential park site agreement; (c) their spouses and
-- domestic partners. reg 4(1)(a) stops at (vii), so the spouse or domestic partner of a beneficiary under (viii) is in
-- no class: that choice is listed on its own and is not an owner's capacity (finding 22).
-- s 2(3)(b): the capacities of a tenant. (i) "a tenant specified in a residential tenancy agreement relating to the
-- premises"; (ii) reg 4(2)(a) a right of occupancy under a residential park tenancy agreement; (b) a rooming house
-- resident under a rooming house agreement; (c) a resident under a resident contract relating to a supported
-- residential facility; (d) a right of occupancy under a written agreement approved by the Minister.
-- Whether an aged persons housing scheme is "approved", or an occupancy agreement approved, by the Minister is a FACT.
DECLARE `Capacity of occupation` IS ONE OF
    `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession`
    `as a sole or joint proprietor of a Crown lease or Crown under lease`
    `as a purchaser of an estate in fee simple paying the price in more than 2 instalments`
    `as the occupier under an agreement to occupy for life, rent-free, liable for all rates and taxes`
    `as a joint proprietor of, or shareholder in a body corporate that owns, a block of home units or other group residential premises`
    `as a lessee or licensee for 5 or more years of land other than Crown land, the premises remaining my property`
    `as the occupier of a house or residential unit in an approved aged persons housing scheme`
    `as a beneficiary under an estate entitling me to occupy in one of the capacities above`
    `as the spouse or domestic partner of a person occupying in one of the capacities above other than as a beneficiary under an estate`
    `as the spouse or domestic partner of a beneficiary under an estate`
    `under a right of occupancy under a residential park site agreement`
    `as the spouse or domestic partner of a person occupying under a residential park site agreement`
    `as a tenant specified in a residential tenancy agreement`
    `under a right of occupancy under a residential park tenancy agreement`
    `as a rooming house resident under a rooming house agreement`
    `as a resident under a resident contract relating to a supported residential facility`
    `under a written occupancy agreement approved by the Minister`
    `in none of these capacities`

-- One person's occupation of one set of premises.
-- s 2(1): "residential premises means premises occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes".
DECLARE `Occupation of premises` HAS
    `the premises are occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises are the person's principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the capacity` IS A `Capacity of occupation`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Capacity of occupation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an owner's capacity under section 2(2)(b)` `c` IF
        `c` EQUALS `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `as a sole or joint proprietor of a Crown lease or Crown under lease`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `as a purchaser of an estate in fee simple paying the price in more than 2 instalments`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `as the occupier under an agreement to occupy for life, rent-free, liable for all rates and taxes`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `as a joint proprietor of, or shareholder in a body corporate that owns, a block of home units or other group residential premises`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `as a lessee or licensee for 5 or more years of land other than Crown land, the premises remaining my property`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `as the occupier of a house or residential unit in an approved aged persons housing scheme`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `as a beneficiary under an estate entitling me to occupy in one of the capacities above`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `as the spouse or domestic partner of a person occupying in one of the capacities above other than as a beneficiary under an estate`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `under a right of occupancy under a residential park site agreement`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `as the spouse or domestic partner of a person occupying under a residential park site agreement`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Capacity of occupation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a tenant's capacity under section 2(3)(b)` `c` IF
        `c` EQUALS `as a tenant specified in a residential tenancy agreement`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `under a right of occupancy under a residential park tenancy agreement`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `as a rooming house resident under a rooming house agreement`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `as a resident under a resident contract relating to a supported residential facility`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `under a written occupancy agreement approved by the Minister`

-- reg 3(2): the "prescribed capacity" for the water rates remission is (a)-(g), the same seven capacities as s 2(2)(b)
-- (i)-(vii), plus (h) "the spouse or domestic partner of any of the persons referred to in paragraphs (a) to (g)" and
-- (i) a beneficiary. It leaves out the residential park site agreement classes of reg 4(1)(b), (c). Like reg 4(1)(a),
-- (h) stops at (g), so the spouse or domestic partner of a beneficiary under (i) is not in a prescribed capacity: that
-- choice is not an owner's capacity either, so this rule leaves it out (finding 22).
GIVEN `c` IS A `Capacity of occupation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a prescribed capacity under regulation 3(2)` `c` IF
        `is an owner's capacity under section 2(2)(b)` `c`
    AND (NOT (`c` EQUALS `under a right of occupancy under a residential park site agreement`))
    AND (NOT (`c` EQUALS `as the spouse or domestic partner of a person occupying under a residential park site agreement`))

-- s 2(2): "a person occupies residential premises as an owner if the person occupies the premises (a) as his or her
-- principal place of residence; and (b) as" one of the capacities.
GIVEN `o` IS AN `Occupation of premises`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person occupies residential premises as an owner` `o` IF
        `o`'s `the premises are occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes`
    AND `o`'s `the premises are the person's principal place of residence`
    AND `is an owner's capacity under section 2(2)(b)` (`o`'s `the capacity`)

-- s 2(3): "a person occupies residential premises as a tenant if the person occupies the premises (a) as his or her
-- principal place of residence; and (b) as" a tenant's capacity.
GIVEN `o` IS AN `Occupation of premises`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person occupies residential premises as a tenant` `o` IF
        `o`'s `the premises are occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes`
    AND `o`'s `the premises are the person's principal place of residence`
    AND `is a tenant's capacity under section 2(3)(b)` (`o`'s `the capacity`)

DECLARE `Way of occupying` IS ONE OF
    `as an owner`
    `as a tenant`
    `neither as an owner nor as a tenant`

GIVEN `o` IS AN `Occupation of premises`
GIVETH A `Way of occupying`
`the way the person occupies the premises` `o` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person occupies residential premises as an owner` `o` THEN `as an owner`
        IF `the person occupies residential premises as a tenant` `o` THEN `as a tenant`
        OTHERWISE `neither as an owner nor as a tenant`

-- reg 3(2): "a person will be taken to occupy land as the person's principal place of residence in a prescribed
-- capacity only if the person occupies the land as the person's principal place of residence" in one of (a)-(i).
GIVEN `o` IS AN `Occupation of premises`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person occupies the land as principal place of residence in a prescribed capacity` `o` IF
        `o`'s `the premises are the person's principal place of residence`
    AND `is a prescribed capacity under regulation 3(2)` (`o`'s `the capacity`)

-- reg 7(3) speaks of "a person referred to in regulation 4(2)(b) or (c)": a rooming house resident, or a resident of a
-- supported residential facility.
GIVEN `o` IS AN `Occupation of premises`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a rooming house or supported residential facility resident` `o` IF
        `o`'s `the capacity` EQUALS `as a rooming house resident under a rooming house agreement`
    OR  `o`'s `the capacity` EQUALS `as a resident under a resident contract relating to a supported residential facility`

§§ `reg 3(1), reg 6 -- the prescribed classes`

-- reg 3(1): "prescribed card means (a) a Pensioner Concession Card issued by the Commonwealth Government; or (b) a Low
-- Income Health Care Card ...; or (c) a TPI Gold Repatriation Health Card ...; or (d) a War Widows Gold Repatriation
-- Health Card ...; or (e) a Gold Repatriation Health Card (EDA) ...; or (f) a Gold Repatriation Health Card issued ...
-- to a person with 80 or more overall impairment points under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 of
-- the Commonwealth; or". The list ends on "or" with nothing after it (finding 3). The Commonwealth Seniors Health Card
-- is not a prescribed card; reg 6(b) names it separately.
GIVEN `c` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a prescribed card` `c` IF
        `c` EQUALS `a Pensioner Concession Card`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a Low Income Health Care Card`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a TPI Gold Repatriation Health Card`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a War Widows Gold Repatriation Health Card`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a Gold Repatriation Health Card (EDA)`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a Gold Repatriation Health Card issued for 80 or more impairment points under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004`

-- reg 3(1): "prescribed payments means (a) any of the following payments under the Social Security Act 1991 of the
-- Commonwealth: (i) an Austudy payment; (ii) a JobSeeker payment; (iii) a parenting payment; (vi) a special benefit;
-- (viii) a youth allowance; or (b) Abstudy payments from the Commonwealth Government; or (c) payments under the
-- Community Development Employment Project or Remote Jobs and Economic Development Program established by the
-- Commonwealth Government; or (d) Self-Employment Assistance allowance payments from the Commonwealth Government; or
-- (e) a pension as a war widow under legislation of the United Kingdom or New Zealand; or (f) farm household allowance
-- payments under the Farm Household Support Act 2014 of the Commonwealth". ((iv), (v) and (vii) were deleted in 2024.)
GIVEN `c` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is one of the prescribed payments` `c` IF
        `c` EQUALS `an Austudy payment`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a JobSeeker payment`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a parenting payment`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a special benefit`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a youth allowance`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `an Abstudy payment`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `payments under the Community Development Employment Project or the Remote Jobs and Economic Development Program`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `Self-Employment Assistance allowance payments`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a war widow's pension under the law of the United Kingdom or New Zealand`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `farm household allowance payments under the Farm Household Support Act 2014`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a prescribed card or prescribed payments` `c` IF
    `is a prescribed card` `c` OR `is one of the prescribed payments` `c`

-- reg 3(1): "low income earner, for a financial year, means a person who, during that financial year, earned income
-- that was less than the amount determined by the Minister for that class of person in relation to that financial year
-- by notice published on the concessions website" (as revised by any later notice). The Minister's amount, and which
-- class of person it is for, are INPUTS; the deposit holds no notice.
GIVEN `income earned during the financial year` IS A NUMBER, `the Minister's amount for the person's class` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a low income earner for the financial year` IF
    `income earned during the financial year` LESS THAN `the Minister's amount for the person's class`

-- The person's position on 1 July of the financial year (s 3(1)), with the year's income for "low income earner".
-- "relevant asylum seeker" (reg 3(1)): a person seeking recognition as a refugee who holds, has applied for, or has
-- held (and holds no other visa) a bridging visa E, or receives Status Resolution Support Service support: a FACT.
DECLARE `Person on 1 July` HAS
    `occupation` IS AN `Occupation of premises`
    `card or payment` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment`
    `is a relevant asylum seeker` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is eligible for a South Australian support package for persons fleeing international conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
    `income earned during the financial year` IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister's low income amount for the person's class` IS A NUMBER

-- reg 6: "(a) holders of a prescribed card; (b) holders of a Commonwealth Seniors Health Card issued by the
-- Commonwealth Government; (c) persons in receipt of prescribed payments; (d) low income earners; (e) relevant asylum
-- seekers; (f) persons eligible for a support package for persons fleeing international conflict provided by the
-- South Australian Government."
GIVEN `p` IS A `Person on 1 July`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is of a class prescribed by regulation 6` `p` IF
        `is a prescribed card` (`p`'s `card or payment`)
    OR  `p`'s `card or payment` EQUALS `a Commonwealth Seniors Health Card`
    OR  `is one of the prescribed payments` (`p`'s `card or payment`)
    OR  `the person is a low income earner for the financial year` (`p`'s `income earned during the financial year`) (`p`'s `the Minister's low income amount for the person's class`)
    OR  `p`'s `is a relevant asylum seeker`
    OR  `p`'s `is eligible for a South Australian support package for persons fleeing international conflict`

§§ `s 3(1) -- the eligible person`

-- s 3(1): "A person is an eligible person for a financial year if, on 1 July of that financial year, the person (a)
-- occupied residential premises as an owner or tenant of the premises; and (b) was of a class prescribed by the
-- regulations for the purposes of this subsection."
GIVEN `p` IS A `Person on 1 July`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an eligible person for the financial year` `p` IF
        (    `the person occupies residential premises as an owner` (`p`'s `occupation`)
         OR  `the person occupies residential premises as a tenant` (`p`'s `occupation`))
    AND `the person is of a class prescribed by regulation 6` `p`

§§ `s 3(2), reg 7 -- entitlement to the concession`

-- The facts reg 7 turns on, for one eligible person, one set of premises and one financial year.
DECLARE `Concession claim` HAS
    `the financial year begins in` IS A NUMBER
    `applied to the Minister before 31 December in the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was paid the concession for the previous financial year for the same premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has been provided with ADI account details for payment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another eligible person has been paid for the financial year for the same premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that other eligible person is a resident in the same room` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has approved splitting the payment with the other eligible person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entered the Switch for Solar program` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the financial year in which the Switch for Solar program was entered begins in` IS A NUMBER
    `received a payment for the financial year in which the Switch for Solar program was entered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has determined that exceptional circumstances lift the Switch for Solar bar for this financial year` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Regulation 8 and the reg 5(5) amounts were substituted from 1 July 2024 (49/2024 r 4, r 6).
GIVEN `the year it begins` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deposited regulations cover the financial year beginning in` `the year it begins` IF
    `the year it begins` AT LEAST 2024

-- reg 7(1)(a): "it is a requirement that the eligible person must have, before 31 December in that financial year,
-- applied to the Minister in a manner and form determined by the Minister (and the application must have been
-- accompanied by any documents or information required by the Minister in connection with the application)"; (2):
-- that requirement "does not apply to an eligible person if the person received a payment under section 3(2) of the Act
-- for the previous financial year in respect of the same residential premises".
GIVEN `paid for the previous financial year for the same premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `regulation 7(2) lifts the application requirement` `paid for the previous financial year for the same premises` IF
    `paid for the previous financial year for the same premises`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Concession claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application requirement is met` `c` IF
        `c`'s `applied to the Minister before 31 December in the financial year`
    OR  `regulation 7(2) lifts the application requirement` (`c`'s `was paid the concession for the previous financial year for the same premises`)

-- reg 7(1)(b): "the Minister has been provided with ADI account details which will allow the payment ... to be made to
-- the person by electronic funds transfer".
GIVEN `c` IS A `Concession claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the account requirement is met` `c` IF
    `c`'s `the Minister has been provided with ADI account details for payment`

-- reg 7(1)(c): "no other eligible person has been given a payment under section 3(2) of the Act for that financial year
-- in respect of the same residential premises"; (3): that requirement "does not apply to an eligible person who is a
-- person referred to in regulation 4(2)(b) or (c) ... unless the other eligible person ... is a resident in the same
-- room as the relevant person".
GIVEN `o` IS AN `Occupation of premises`, `c` IS A `Concession claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the one payment per premises requirement is met` `o` `c` IF
        (NOT (`c`'s `another eligible person has been paid for the financial year for the same premises`))
    OR  (    `the person is a rooming house or supported residential facility resident` `o`
         AND (NOT (`c`'s `that other eligible person is a resident in the same room`)))

-- reg 7(3aa): "Despite the requirement set out in subregulation (1)(c), the Minister may, if the Minister considers
-- that it is appropriate in the circumstances, approve that payment of a concession to an eligible person be split, in
-- the manner determined by the Minister, between the eligible person and 1 or more other eligible persons who reside at
-- the same residential premises." The approval and the split are the Minister's: INPUT, answered conditionally.
GIVEN `o` IS AN `Occupation of premises`, `c` IS A `Concession claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment is split under regulation 7(3aa)` `o` `c` IF
        (NOT (`the one payment per premises requirement is met` `o` `c`))
    AND `c`'s `the Minister has approved splitting the payment with the other eligible person`

-- reg 7(3a): a person who, in a financial year (the relevant financial year), "enters into the Switch for Solar program
-- administered by the State Government for the installation of solar panels is not eligible for a payment ... (a) for
-- the relevant financial year; and (b) (i) in the case of a person who receives or received a payment for the relevant
-- financial year (despite not being eligible for the payment under paragraph (a))--for each of the 10 financial years
-- following the relevant financial year; or (ii) in any other case--for each of the 9 financial years following".
-- (3c): "The Minister may determine that subregulation (3a) does not apply to a person in relation to a particular
-- financial year if satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist" (INPUT).
GIVEN `c` IS A `Concession claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of following years barred by Switch for Solar` `c` MEANS
    IF `c`'s `received a payment for the financial year in which the Switch for Solar program was entered`
    THEN 10
    ELSE 9

-- (3a)(a): the first year barred is "the relevant financial year", the year the program was entered.
GIVEN `c` IS A `Concession claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first financial year barred by Switch for Solar begins in` `c` MEANS
    `c`'s `the financial year in which the Switch for Solar program was entered begins in`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Concession claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last financial year barred by Switch for Solar begins in` `c` MEANS
    `the first financial year barred by Switch for Solar begins in` `c`
        PLUS `the number of following years barred by Switch for Solar` `c`

-- The years reg 7(3a) bars, before any (3c) determination for a particular year.
DECLARE `Switch for Solar bar` IS ONE OF
    `barred for the financial years beginning in` HAS
        `the first` IS A NUMBER
        `the last` IS A NUMBER
    `not barred: the Switch for Solar program was not entered`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Concession claim`
GIVETH A `Switch for Solar bar`
`the financial years barred by Switch for Solar` `c` MEANS
    IF `c`'s `entered the Switch for Solar program`
    THEN `barred for the financial years beginning in` (`the first financial year barred by Switch for Solar begins in` `c`) (`the last financial year barred by Switch for Solar begins in` `c`)
    ELSE `not barred: the Switch for Solar program was not entered`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Concession claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is barred by the Switch for Solar program` `c` IF
        `c`'s `entered the Switch for Solar program`
    AND `c`'s `the financial year begins in` AT LEAST `the first financial year barred by Switch for Solar begins in` `c`
    AND `c`'s `the financial year begins in` AT MOST `the last financial year barred by Switch for Solar begins in` `c`
    AND (NOT (`c`'s `the Minister has determined that exceptional circumstances lift the Switch for Solar bar for this financial year`))

DECLARE `Why no concession` IS ONE OF
    `not an eligible person: on 1 July I did not occupy residential premises as an owner or tenant`
    `not an eligible person: on 1 July I was not of a prescribed class`
    `I did not apply before 31 December and was not paid last year for the same premises`
    `the Minister has not been given my ADI account details`
    `the Switch for Solar program bars me this year`
    `another eligible person has been paid this year for the same premises`

DECLARE `Concession entitlement` IS ONE OF
    `entitled to the concession`
    `entitled to the share of the concession the Minister has approved under regulation 7(3aa)`
    `not entitled` HAS `because` IS A `Why no concession`
    `not covered: the deposited regulations apply from the 2024/2025 financial year`

-- s 3(2): "A person who (a) is an eligible person for a financial year; and (b) satisfies the eligibility requirements
-- prescribed by the regulations, is entitled to payment by the Minister of an amount determined in accordance with the
-- regulations in respect of that financial year."
GIVEN `p` IS A `Person on 1 July`, `c` IS A `Concession claim`
GIVETH A `Concession entitlement`
`the person's entitlement to the concession` `p` `c` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the deposited regulations cover the financial year beginning in` (`c`'s `the financial year begins in`))
            THEN `not covered: the deposited regulations apply from the 2024/2025 financial year`
        IF NOT (    `the person occupies residential premises as an owner` (`p`'s `occupation`)
                OR  `the person occupies residential premises as a tenant` (`p`'s `occupation`))
            THEN `not entitled` `not an eligible person: on 1 July I did not occupy residential premises as an owner or tenant`
        IF NOT (`the person is of a class prescribed by regulation 6` `p`)
            THEN `not entitled` `not an eligible person: on 1 July I was not of a prescribed class`
        IF NOT (`the application requirement is met` `c`)
            THEN `not entitled` `I did not apply before 31 December and was not paid last year for the same premises`
        IF NOT (`the account requirement is met` `c`)
            THEN `not entitled` `the Minister has not been given my ADI account details`
        IF `the person is barred by the Switch for Solar program` `c`
            THEN `not entitled` `the Switch for Solar program bars me this year`
        IF `the payment is split under regulation 7(3aa)` (`p`'s `occupation`) `c`
            THEN `entitled to the share of the concession the Minister has approved under regulation 7(3aa)`
        IF NOT (`the one payment per premises requirement is met` (`p`'s `occupation`) `c`)
            THEN `not entitled` `another eligible person has been paid this year for the same premises`
        OTHERWISE `entitled to the concession`

-- reg 7(1)(a): the last day to apply. "before 31 December in that financial year": the last day is 30 December of the
-- calendar year in which the financial year begins.
GIVEN `the year it begins` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for the concession for the financial year beginning in` `the year it begins` MEANS
    YMD `the year it begins` 12 30

-- reg 7(1)(a), (2): by what day the person must apply, if at all.
DECLARE `Application deadline` IS ONE OF
    `apply on or before` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no application needed: paid the concession for the previous financial year for the same premises`
    `not covered: the deposited regulations apply from the 2024/2025 financial year`

GIVEN `the year it begins` IS A NUMBER, `paid for the previous financial year for the same premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Application deadline`
`the application deadline for the financial year beginning in` `the year it begins` `paid for the previous financial year for the same premises` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the deposited regulations cover the financial year beginning in` `the year it begins`)
            THEN `not covered: the deposited regulations apply from the 2024/2025 financial year`
        IF `regulation 7(2) lifts the application requirement` `paid for the previous financial year for the same premises`
            THEN `no application needed: paid the concession for the previous financial year for the same premises`
        OTHERWISE `apply on or before` (`the last day to apply for the concession for the financial year beginning in` `the year it begins`)

§§ `reg 3(3), (4), reg 8 -- the amount, indexed`

-- reg 8: "The amount to be paid to an eligible person in respect of a financial year in accordance with section 3(2) of
-- the Act is determined to be $255.60 (indexed)."
`the concession amount stated in regulation 8` MEANS 255.60

-- reg 5(5): "prescribed maximum remission for a financial year means--$377.00 (indexed); prescribed minimum remission
-- for a financial year means--$236.40 (indexed)".
`the prescribed maximum remission stated in regulation 5(5)` MEANS 377.00
`the prescribed minimum remission stated in regulation 5(5)` MEANS 236.40

-- The CPI figures reg 3(3) uses: "the Consumer Price Index (All groups index for Adelaide) published by the Australian
-- Bureau of Statistics". They are INPUTS (no ABS figure is deposited).
DECLARE `Indexation figures` HAS
    `the financial year begins in` IS A NUMBER
    `the CPI for the December quarter of the year before the financial year begins` IS A NUMBER
    `the CPI for the December quarter of 2023` IS A NUMBER

-- reg 3(3): an amount followed by "(indexed)" is "adjusted on 1 July of each year beginning on 1 July 2021, by
-- multiplying the stated amount by a multiplier obtained by dividing the CPI for the December quarter of the
-- immediately preceding year by the CPI for the December quarter of 2023 (with the amount so adjusted being rounded up
-- to the nearest multiple of 10 cents)". For the financial year beginning 1 July 2024 the "immediately preceding year"
-- is 2023, so the multiplier is the December 2023 quarter divided by itself: 1, whatever figure is given.
GIVEN `f` IS AN `Indexation figures`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the regulation 3(3) multiplier` `f` MEANS
    IF `f`'s `the financial year begins in` EQUALS 2024
    THEN 1
    ELSE `f`'s `the CPI for the December quarter of the year before the financial year begins` DIVIDED BY `f`'s `the CPI for the December quarter of 2023`

-- reg 3(4): "If an amount to be remitted or paid in a financial year is, when adjusted in accordance with subregulation
-- (3), less than the amount remitted or paid in the immediately preceding financial year, the amount to be remitted or
-- paid will not be the amount as adjusted ..., but will instead be an amount equal to the amount remitted or paid in the
-- immediately preceding financial year." The previous year's amount is an INPUT.
GIVEN `the stated amount` IS A NUMBER, `f` IS AN `Indexation figures`, `the amount for the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the indexed amount` `the stated amount` `f` `the amount for the previous financial year` MEANS
    IF `adjusted` LESS THAN `the amount for the previous financial year`
    THEN `the amount for the previous financial year`
    ELSE `adjusted`
    WHERE
        `adjusted` MEANS `rounded up to the nearest 10 cents` (`the stated amount` TIMES `the regulation 3(3) multiplier` `f`)

GIVEN `f` IS AN `Indexation figures`, `the amount paid for the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the concession amount for the financial year` `f` `the amount paid for the previous financial year` MEANS
    `the indexed amount` `the concession amount stated in regulation 8` `f` `the amount paid for the previous financial year`

§§ `s 4, reg 5 -- remission of water rates`

-- reg 3(1): "water rates means (a) rates under the Irrigation Act 2009; or (b) rates under the Renmark Irrigation Trust
-- Act 2009" (finding 9). The ratepayer's position for one parcel of land and one financial year.
-- reg 5(5): "relevant date means (a) the date on which the person is billed with the rates; or (b) the date on which the
-- rates are payable by the person."
DECLARE `Water rates position` HAS
    `the water rates for the land for the financial year` IS A NUMBER
    `the ratepayer's proportion of interest in the land` IS A NUMBER
    `the ratepayer occupies the land as principal place of residence in a prescribed capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse or domestic partner also occupies the land as principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ratepayer holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date billed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ratepayer holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date payable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse or domestic partner holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date billed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse or domestic partner holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date payable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ratepayer was entitled to a remission of water rates for the preceding rating period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied by a means test that the ratepayer suffers exceptional circumstances of hardship` IS A BOOLEAN

-- reg 5(1)(a): "(i) the ratepayer holds a prescribed card or is in receipt of prescribed payments; and (ii) the
-- ratepayer occupies the land as the ratepayer's principal place of residence in a prescribed capacity"; (b): "(i) the
-- spouse or domestic partner of the ratepayer holds a prescribed card or is in receipt of prescribed payments; and (ii)
-- the ratepayer and the ratepayer's spouse or domestic partner occupy the land as their principal place of residence in
-- a prescribed capacity". READING: the occupation is taken to be the same on both relevant dates; only the card or
-- payment is asked date by date.
GIVEN `w` IS A `Water rates position`, `on the date billed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `regulation 5(1)(a) or (b) is satisfied on the date` `w` `on the date billed` IF
        (    `ratepayer holds`
         AND `w`'s `the ratepayer occupies the land as principal place of residence in a prescribed capacity`)
    OR  (    `spouse holds`
         AND `w`'s `the ratepayer occupies the land as principal place of residence in a prescribed capacity`
         AND `w`'s `the spouse or domestic partner also occupies the land as principal place of residence`)
    WHERE
        `ratepayer holds` MEANS
            IF `on the date billed`
            THEN `w`'s `the ratepayer holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date billed`
            ELSE `w`'s `the ratepayer holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date payable`
        `spouse holds` MEANS
            IF `on the date billed`
            THEN `w`'s `the spouse or domestic partner holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date billed`
            ELSE `w`'s `the spouse or domestic partner holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date payable`

-- reg 5(1): entitled "if (a) on the relevant date ... or (b) on the relevant date ... or (c) at the time of recovery of
-- the rates (i) the ratepayer satisfies the Minister, by submitting to a means test determined by the Minister, that the
-- ratepayer is suffering exceptional circumstances of hardship; and (ii) the ratepayer occupies the land as the
-- ratepayer's principal place of residence in a prescribed capacity". (2): "A ratepayer who satisfies the conditions set
-- out in subregulation (1)(a) or (b) on the date on which the rates are payable by the ratepayer but not on the date on
-- which the ratepayer is billed with the rates must, in addition, have been entitled to a remission of water rates for
-- the preceding rating period in respect of the same or different land."
-- s 4(3): "A ratepayer who, in the opinion of the Minister, complies with the prescribed criteria is entitled to a
-- remission". This rule says whether the criteria are met; the entitlement then rests on the Minister's opinion.
GIVEN `w` IS A `Water rates position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ratepayer meets the regulation 5 criteria for a remission of water rates` `w` IF
        `regulation 5(1)(a) or (b) is satisfied on the date` `w` TRUE
    OR  (    `regulation 5(1)(a) or (b) is satisfied on the date` `w` FALSE
         AND `w`'s `the ratepayer was entitled to a remission of water rates for the preceding rating period`)
    OR  (    `w`'s `the Minister is satisfied by a means test that the ratepayer suffers exceptional circumstances of hardship`
         AND `w`'s `the ratepayer occupies the land as principal place of residence in a prescribed capacity`)

-- reg 5(4): "The amount of the remission of water rates for land for a financial year is 30% of the amount of the
-- rates, subject to the prescribed minimum remission and the prescribed maximum remission for that year." READING: a
-- remission cannot exceed the rates, so where the minimum is more than the rates the whole of the rates is remitted
-- (finding 11).
GIVEN `the rates` IS A NUMBER, `the minimum` IS A NUMBER, `the maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the remission of water rates for the land` `the rates` `the minimum` `the maximum` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `the rates` `and` (`the lesser of` `the maximum` `and` (`the greater of` `the minimum` `and` (`the rates` TIMES 30%)))

-- reg 5(3): "If 2 or more persons own land jointly or as tenants in common, each of them who is entitled to a remission
-- of water rates for the land is entitled to a proportion of the amount of the remission equal to the proportion of the
-- person's interest in the land." A sole owner's proportion is 1.
GIVEN `w` IS A `Water rates position`, `the minimum` IS A NUMBER, `the maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ratepayer's remission of water rates` `w` `the minimum` `the maximum` MEANS
    IF `the ratepayer meets the regulation 5 criteria for a remission of water rates` `w`
    THEN `w`'s `the ratepayer's proportion of interest in the land`
             TIMES `the remission of water rates for the land` (`w`'s `the water rates for the land for the financial year`) `the minimum` `the maximum`
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 7, s 8 -- interest, the duty to tell the Minister, refunds and penalties`

-- s 7(1): "No interest, fine or other penalty is payable in respect of rates remitted by this Act."
`the interest, fine or penalty payable on rates remitted` MEANS 0

-- s 7(2): "No interest is payable by the Minister in respect of an amount to which a person is entitled under this
-- Act."
`the interest the Minister pays on a concession` MEANS 0

-- s 8(2) and s 8(3): "Maximum penalty: $2 500."
`the maximum penalty under section 8(2) or (3)` MEANS 2500

§§ `Regulative rules -- the person and the Minister`

DECLARE `Concession party` IS ONE OF `the person`, `the Minister`

DECLARE `Concession act` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the Minister for the concession`
    `pay the concession` HAS `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `inform the Minister in writing that a remission criterion is no longer satisfied`
    `inform the Minister in writing of a payment the person was not entitled to receive`
    `refund the payment to the Minister` HAS `the amount refunded` IS A NUMBER

-- s 3(2): the person "is entitled to payment by the Minister of an amount determined in accordance with the
-- regulations". No time is set for the Minister; s 7(2): no interest is payable if it is late.
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Concession party` `Concession act`
DECIDE `s 3(2) -- the Minister must pay the concession` `the amount` IS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MUST  `pay the concession` (EXACTLY `the amount`)

-- reg 7(1)(a), (2): apply before 31 December (on or before 30 December), unless paid last year for the same premises.
-- Clock: days, counted from 1 July of the financial year. Applying is the person's choice: not applying is no breach,
-- but the concession is then not payable (DO ... LEST FULFILLED). The rule assumes the other reg 7 requirements are met
-- (see `the person's entitlement to the concession`).
GIVEN `the year it begins` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from 1 July to the last day to apply` `the year it begins` MEANS
    `days from` (`1 July of the financial year beginning in` `the year it begins`) `to` (`the last day to apply for the concession for the financial year beginning in` `the year it begins`)

GIVEN `the year it begins` IS A NUMBER, `paid last year for the same premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Concession party` `Concession act`
DECIDE `reg 7(1)(a), (2) -- apply before 31 December, unless paid last year for the same premises; then the Minister must pay` `the year it begins` `paid last year for the same premises` `the amount` IS
    IF `regulation 7(2) lifts the application requirement` `paid last year for the same premises`
    THEN `s 3(2) -- the Minister must pay the concession` `the amount`
    ELSE PARTY `the person`
         DO    `apply to the Minister for the concession`
         WITHIN `the days from 1 July to the last day to apply` `the year it begins`
         HENCE `s 3(2) -- the Minister must pay the concession` `the amount`
         LEST  FULFILLED

-- s 8(2): "A person who has received remission of rates under this Act but who ceases to satisfy any one of the
-- criteria on which the remission was based shall inform the Minister in writing of that fact. Maximum penalty:
-- $2 500." The Act sets no time: the days allowed are an INPUT (a court would decide whether the person informed the
-- Minister in time). Clock: days from ceasing to satisfy the criterion.
GIVEN `received a remission and ceased to satisfy a criterion` IS A BOOLEAN, `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Concession party` `Concession act`
DECIDE `s 8(2) -- tell the Minister in writing on ceasing to meet a remission criterion` `received a remission and ceased to satisfy a criterion` `the days allowed` IS
    IF `received a remission and ceased to satisfy a criterion`
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         MUST  `inform the Minister in writing that a remission criterion is no longer satisfied`
         WITHIN `the days allowed`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "s 8(2): a person who has received a remission of rates and ceases to satisfy a criterion must inform the Minister in writing; maximum penalty $2 500"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 8(3): "A person who has received a payment under this Act that the person is not entitled to receive must (a)
-- inform the Minister, in writing, of that fact; and (b) refund the amount of the payment to the Minister in accordance
-- with any directions of the Minister. Maximum penalty: $2 500." (4): "If a person has received a payment under this
-- Act that the person is not entitled to receive, the amount of the payment is recoverable as a debt due to the
-- Minister." No time is set for (a): an INPUT. The time for (b) is the Minister's direction: an INPUT. Clock: days from
-- when the person learns the payment was not due.
GIVEN `the amount received` IS A NUMBER, `the days allowed to inform` IS A NUMBER, `the days the Minister's directions allow to refund` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Concession party` `Concession act`
DECIDE `s 8(3), (4) -- tell the Minister and refund a payment not entitled to` `the amount received` `the days allowed to inform` `the days the Minister's directions allow to refund` IS
        (PARTY `the person`
         MUST  `inform the Minister in writing of a payment the person was not entitled to receive`
         WITHIN `the days allowed to inform`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "s 8(3)(a): a person paid a concession not due must inform the Minister in writing; maximum penalty $2 500")
    RAND
        (PARTY `the person`
         MUST  `refund the payment to the Minister` (EXACTLY `the amount received`)
         WITHIN `the days the Minister's directions allow to refund`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "s 8(3)(b): a person paid a concession not due must refund it as the Minister directs; maximum penalty $2 500; s 8(4): the amount is recoverable as a debt due to the Minister")

-- s 8(4), with reg 7(3b): what the Minister can recover as a debt. reg 7(3b): "Despite subregulation (3a)(a), a person
-- who has already received a payment under section 3(2) of the Act for the relevant financial year is not required to
-- return the payment." READING: such a payment is not one to be refunded or recovered (finding 6).
GIVEN `the amount received` IS A NUMBER, `the person was entitled to it` IS A BOOLEAN, `it was received before entering Switch for Solar in the same financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount recoverable as a debt due to the Minister` `the amount received` `the person was entitled to it` `it was received before entering Switch for Solar in the same financial year` MEANS
    IF `the person was entitled to it` OR `it was received before entering Switch for Solar in the same financial year`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the amount received`
